== pgcopydb: e-w1 -> e-w2, PostgreSQL 18 ==

-- latency: 1000 single-row transactions, one session, 50 ms apart
p50 0.7 ms, p95 2.2 ms, p99 5.2 ms, rows 1000

-- throughput: pgbench, 8 clients, 30 s, one insert per transaction
   source: tps = 84891.634009 (without initial connection time)
   source committed 2547043 rows; 313163 were on the target when the load stopped; the rest took 109.9 s more
   target applied 18206 rows/s over the whole run, 10438 rows/s while it was loaded

-- one transaction of 1000000 rows
   committed on the source after 1.0 s, complete on the target 7.3 s after that

-- one UPDATE statement of 1000000 rows: update events set payload = payload (REPLICA IDENTITY FULL)
   committed on the source after 15.1 s, complete on the target 13.6 s after that
